From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:38:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: mask the GMAC interrupt while the data plane is
 claimed

The claim parks the host DMA and NAPI, but the NSS firmware drives the
same DMA and the GMAC line stays requested by stmmac: every frame the
firmware moves raised a host interrupt that stmmac_interrupt() counted as
a normal DMA interrupt and could not act on, since with NAPI disabled it
never masks the channel. Measured on IPQ5018 under Wi-Fi load: 7495
interrupts in 10 s, 7283 of them normal_irq_n. Mask the line at the host
from claim to release; the owner releases before any close or reopen.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
---
 .../net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c   | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index f3c385df6..eca07a47d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -2573,9 +2573,10 @@ static void stmmac_stop_all_dma(struct stmmac_priv *priv)
  * @owner: callbacks taking over TX and receiving link transitions
  * @ctx: cookie passed back through every callback
  *
- * Parks the host data path (TX drained, NAPI off, DMA channels stopped)
- * and redirects ndo_start_xmit to @owner->xmit. The MAC stays enabled and
- * phylink keeps managing the link; transitions are relayed through
+ * Parks the host data path (TX drained, NAPI off, DMA channels stopped,
+ * the GMAC interrupt masked) and redirects ndo_start_xmit to @owner->xmit.
+ * The MAC stays enabled and phylink keeps managing the link; transitions
+ * are relayed through
  * @owner->link_up/link_down. Caller holds rtnl. See qca_dwmac.h for the
  * release contract.
  */
@@ -2607,6 +2608,11 @@ int qca_dwmac_dp_claim(struct net_device *dev,
 	netif_tx_disable(dev);
 	stmmac_disable_all_queues(priv);
 	stmmac_stop_all_dma(priv);
+	/*
+	 * The firmware's DMA keeps raising the GMAC interrupt, once per frame
+	 * with NAPI parked: mask it at the host until release.
+	 */
+	disable_irq(dev->irq);
 
 	priv->dp_ctx = ctx;
 	/* xmit hook reads dp_owner without a lock: publish ctx first */
@@ -2647,6 +2653,7 @@ int qca_dwmac_dp_release(struct net_device *dev)
 	netif_tx_disable(dev);
 	WRITE_ONCE(priv->dp_owner, NULL);
 	priv->dp_ctx = NULL;
+	enable_irq(dev->irq);
 
 	/*
 	 * Claim parked NAPI with stmmac_disable_all_queues(); give it back
@@ -2654,8 +2661,8 @@ int qca_dwmac_dp_release(struct net_device *dev)
 	 * interface going down, or the caller's restorative dev_close() -
 	 * will disable it again, and a second napi_disable() without an
 	 * enable in between blocks forever (measured: reboot hangs right
-	 * after "Link is Down"). The DMA channels stay stopped and no IRQs
-	 * are live, so the re-enabled NAPI sits idle until then.
+	 * after "Link is Down"). The DMA channels stay stopped, so the
+	 * re-enabled NAPI sits idle until then.
 	 */
 	stmmac_enable_all_queues(priv);
 
